{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113280245507751936"]}, "author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-22T14:44:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113280305301971067"], "id": "2113280305301971067", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 54, "impression_count": 16941, "like_count": 73, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 16}, "text": "Looking Ahead\n\nModeling Future Evolution in Autoregressive Video Generation\n\npaper: https://t.co/DRdK9bigNZ https://t.co/jQRbx7m2et", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2113280305301971067"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["16_2113278096610660352"]}, "author_id": "4783690002", "created_at": "2026-10-22T14:38:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113278710795153785"], "id": "2113278710795153785", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 199, "impression_count": 64112, "like_count": 716, "quote_count": 50, "reply_count": 127, "retweet_count": 85}, "text": "Not all forests are equal, and now we can map the difference. 🌳\n\nMeet Forest Typology (ForTy): a 10m map of natural, planted, and farmed forests to help identify deforestation and protect the forests that matter most. 🧵 https://t.co/JoIOTkiZcT", "url": "https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2113278710795153785"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-22T12:53:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113252328169951372"], "id": "2113252328169951372", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 33097, "like_count": 282, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "I don’t know if it’s an internet scale disaster yet, but it’s definitely the biggest stress test we’ve had.", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2113252328169951372"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-22T11:31:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113231789321838934"], "id": "2113231789321838934", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 19, "impression_count": 14026, "like_count": 149, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 24, "retweet_count": 27}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2107840567040262624", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The point of this is that the balance of having open models help with cyber defense, and the trajectory we’re on being well more fine than people think.\n\nIt’s not that open weights won’t be used in cyber attacks. All possible AI trajectories had many cyber incidents imo. \n\nLike https://t.co/8sp5P56tbe", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2113231789321838934"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113081717288263680"]}, "author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-22T01:35:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113081719817380193"], "id": "2113081719817380193", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 92, "impression_count": 45148, "like_count": 273, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 36}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112890642590564386", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Japan’s wave of corporate breaches is the latest sign that AI is changing how hacking works.\n\nSince Sept 25, 18 Japanese companies have disclosed breaches, including Tokyo Metro, Japan Post, Lawson, Nikkei, Yamato and Sagawa. Attackers got about 6.6M Times Car accounts, some with https://t.co/42Sa1CwPcM https://t.co/TqIBbtQuN1", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2113081719817380193"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113054574114115584"]}, "author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-21T23:47:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113054576844628113"], "id": "2113054576844628113", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 56, "impression_count": 27415, "like_count": 151, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "Three teams in one month have pushed LLM decode forward with megakernels: Inferact on Google TPUs, AMD with TileRT and FlyDSL, and now NVIDIA on GB300, now live on InferenceX.\n\nWe're excited to see these gains and dig into the engineering behind faster inference.\n\nMegakernels https://t.co/uRbkLfrA2J", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2113054576844628113"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-21T23:14:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113046396311859238"], "id": "2113046396311859238", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 24, "impression_count": 20383, "like_count": 261, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "What a wild day. We have a lot of work to do to get through this llm transition. But still, feels like the AI world will get crazier and scarier before it gets better. I hope I'm wrong, but my current emotion is something like... \"gulp.\"", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2113046396311859238"}, {"author_id": "778764142412984320", "created_at": "2026-10-21T22:49:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113039952963641570"], "id": "2113039952963641570", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 192, "impression_count": 47135, "like_count": 390, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 26, "retweet_count": 25}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113038595854623029", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Come and build models, datasets, and spaces on the hub, to win $20k in cash and credits! https://t.co/QQHsFaoFX9", "url": "https://x.com/huggingface/status/2113039952963641570"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "13_2113280245507751936", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "16_2113278096610660352", "type": "animated_gif"}, {"media_key": "3_2113081717288263680", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113054574114115584", "type": "photo"}], "users": [{"id": "2465283662", "name": "AK", "username": "_akhaliq"}, {"id": "4783690002", "name": "Google DeepMind", "username": "GoogleDeepMind"}, {"id": "2939913921", "name": "Nathan Lambert", "username": "natolambert"}, {"id": "1745106082790318080", "name": "SemiAnalysis", "username": "SemiAnalysis_"}, {"id": "778764142412984320", "name": "Hugging Face", "username": "huggingface"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2113280305301971067", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlwtimwlgrihdgqru055ylkon6nx", "oldest_id": "2113039952963641570", "result_count": 8}}
